  "foaf:name": "Programa Caletas Sustentables",
  "sdo:name": "Programa Caletas Sustentables",
  "sdo:description": "Caletas Sustentables is a national project launched in 2019 to support artisanal fishing communities across Chile in accelerating the transition toward sustainable coastal livelihoods. The project operates through a national collaboration network and targeted investments that contribute to the environmental, social and economic sustainability of artisanal fishing coves. It supports community-led initiatives and innovative solutions that emerge from fishing organizations themselves and strengthens local capacities through expert support and technology transfer by actors present in the territory. The project has been already implemented in coastal communities in Aysén, Los Lagos, Valparaíso, Coquimbo and Antofagasta regions, with a national scope and potential for replication, contributing to healthier oceans and more resilient coastal communities.",
